message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "MiDM: Minimal Decision Models and an audit of CLM-8B"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yoon"
    given-names: "YeoHoon"
    affiliation: "Seoul School of Integrated Sciences and Technologies, Seoul, KR"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2669-8127"
license: Apache-2.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23084584"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
keywords:
  - decision model
  - typed decisions
  - LoRA
  - pointer head
  - reproducibility
  - evaluation audit
abstract: >-
  Code and results for a controlled study of small (8B or fewer parameters) typed-decision models (MiDM:
  LoRA-tuned causal LMs with a pointer head over option lines). The work includes an exact reproduction and
  statistical audit of the CLM-8B DeepSWE verifier claim, and it identifies which factors matter for transfer:
  base-model generation and balanced data breadth. Adapter variants, TTA, calibration and ensembles did not.
